[{:db/id 17592186152199 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-34094a62-379f-5750-81e2-774654924818"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-34094a62-379f-5750-81e2-774654924818" :question/id #uuid "34094a62-379f-5750-81e2-774654924818" :question/math-academy-id "q-80505" :question/problem "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curve ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1.$ If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y), & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,{∬}_{D}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of the rectangular domain $R?$\n\nI. $R=[-1,1]\\times [-1,1]$\n\nII. $R=[-1,1]\\times [0,1]$\n\nIII. $R=[-2,2]\\times [-2,2]$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D:$\n\n![](images/c5/c50e0e01d432b1db736fad09dd5f5b82286e981d88586e848d9b57c8a9910eb0.png)\n\nNotice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y), & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given rectangles.\n\n- Rectangle II does not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Rectangles I and III covers the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ee7f980b-3738-5f95-89d8-bd69eb485ba5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ee7f980b-3738-5f95-89d8-bd69eb485ba5" :answer-field/id #uuid "ee7f980b-3738-5f95-89d8-bd69eb485ba5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ae28b501-c23e-599b-8e7e-1db8502ac7b0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-396e3f27-e24a-553a-9d76-87b06e254ca7" "answer-ae28b501-c23e-599b-8e7e-1db8502ac7b0" "answer-4facf5d2-11cf-5ead-aac1-8f2480139664" "answer-d970f7e7-4967-5568-882e-bad44890c0c5" "answer-cf5cd3c6-1bfc-586c-9f3c-4788cef42fad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-396e3f27-e24a-553a-9d76-87b06e254ca7" :answer/id #uuid "396e3f27-e24a-553a-9d76-87b06e254ca7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae28b501-c23e-599b-8e7e-1db8502ac7b0" :answer/id #uuid "ae28b501-c23e-599b-8e7e-1db8502ac7b0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4facf5d2-11cf-5ead-aac1-8f2480139664" :answer/id #uuid "4facf5d2-11cf-5ead-aac1-8f2480139664" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d970f7e7-4967-5568-882e-bad44890c0c5" :answer/id #uuid "d970f7e7-4967-5568-882e-bad44890c0c5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf5cd3c6-1bfc-586c-9f3c-4788cef42fad" :answer/id #uuid "cf5cd3c6-1bfc-586c-9f3c-4788cef42fad" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186348410 :question/problem "![](images/50/506a298041a875549ec60c5cf99ebdbeb5ca4b5717037083fa6ca196fce27279.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If $R=[-2,2]\\times [0,3],$ and\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{2x+y}{y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of $f(x,y)?$\n\nI. $\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+y}{y}, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin D\\end{aligned}$\n\nII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & (x,y)\\in R \\\\ \\frac{2x+y}{y}, & (x,y)\\in D∖R\\end{aligned}$\n\nIII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+y}{y}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152200 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f7e910b3-a1a9-5ea8-8009-6cb31a154137"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f7e910b3-a1a9-5ea8-8009-6cb31a154137" :question/id #uuid "f7e910b3-a1a9-5ea8-8009-6cb31a154137" :question/math-academy-id "q-86864" :question/problem "![](images/bb/bbc1bc7b3bb910ffbd13571283bbfa305404d13eb2cb3b5ab423a1c02e46ab86.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}) & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true? \n\nI. ${∬}_{R}y({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-1,1]\\times [0,2]$\n\nII. ${∬}_{D}y({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,2]$\n\nIII. ${∬}_{D}y({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-1,2]\\times [-2,2]$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}), & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}y({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statement II is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement III is false. The rectangle $R$ does not cover the region $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3db2d41e-f30d-5228-a8d5-a3f179326943"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3db2d41e-f30d-5228-a8d5-a3f179326943" :answer-field/id #uuid "3db2d41e-f30d-5228-a8d5-a3f179326943" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5932c78c-b217-563b-a6a6-20d7e590fa51" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d22715d7-9b30-5b4e-992d-a26755e9bfa5" "answer-f4c01149-e6b5-5a05-a88f-4203104561a0" "answer-f20bd2cc-e250-5b0f-8550-2d109881dffa" "answer-5932c78c-b217-563b-a6a6-20d7e590fa51" "answer-6b2be67b-0fbe-5c0e-9a6c-695744bdced7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d22715d7-9b30-5b4e-992d-a26755e9bfa5" :answer/id #uuid "d22715d7-9b30-5b4e-992d-a26755e9bfa5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4c01149-e6b5-5a05-a88f-4203104561a0" :answer/id #uuid "f4c01149-e6b5-5a05-a88f-4203104561a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f20bd2cc-e250-5b0f-8550-2d109881dffa" :answer/id #uuid "f20bd2cc-e250-5b0f-8550-2d109881dffa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5932c78c-b217-563b-a6a6-20d7e590fa51" :answer/id #uuid "5932c78c-b217-563b-a6a6-20d7e590fa51" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b2be67b-0fbe-5c0e-9a6c-695744bdced7" :answer/id #uuid "6b2be67b-0fbe-5c0e-9a6c-695744bdced7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-e225bb36-aed4-51b2-b84b-6230033e0f20" :activity/id #uuid "e225bb36-aed4-51b2-b84b-6230033e0f20" :activity/title "Double Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049229 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-151f4abe-23c3-58b1-8e53-69be8020bff5" "step-36b5039d-7687-54cd-9c71-0a7c40931970" "step-8d37cf97-1bdd-5ae3-a97c-0f1ffc62d78b"] :activity/first-step "step-151f4abe-23c3-58b1-8e53-69be8020bff5" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-151f4abe-23c3-58b1-8e53-69be8020bff5" :step/id #uuid "151f4abe-23c3-58b1-8e53-69be8020bff5" :step/content "question-34094a62-379f-5750-81e2-774654924818" :step/next "step-36b5039d-7687-54cd-9c71-0a7c40931970" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-36b5039d-7687-54cd-9c71-0a7c40931970" :step/